From: WelsonJS
Subject: [PATCH] Windows build: resources for the tools and MSVC fixes

Windows-specific changes: an icon and version information for the tool
executables, and MSVC options and warnings.

1. tools : Windows icon and version information for the tool executables

  llama.cpp has no Windows resource files, so its executables have no icon and
  no version information (the "Description" in the file properties is empty).

  Add two cache options to tools/CMakeLists.txt:

    - LLAMA_WIN_ICON: an .ico file, embedded as the application icon. It is
      copied next to the resource scripts, which start with
      #pragma code_page(65001), so a build folder with non-ASCII characters
      works regardless of the ANSI code page.
    - LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION: a text for the version information. Each tool gets
      a VERSIONINFO resource with FileDescription "<tool> (<text>)", ProductName
      "llama.cpp", InternalName/OriginalFilename from the target name, and
      FileVersion/ProductVersion 0.0.<LLAMA_BUILD_NUMBER>.0 (<LLAMA_BUILD_COMMIT>).
      The resource uses numeric FILEOS/FILETYPE values instead of the winver.h
      names, so no include path is needed (rc.exe and llvm-rc).

  Every executable target under tools/ gets its own resource script; the DLLs
  get none. The scripts are written through configure_file, which only touches
  a file when its content changes, so a new CMake run does not relink the
  tools. With both options empty (the default) the build is unchanged.

2. ggml-cpu : do not pass unsupported options to MSVC

  Two compiler options in ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt produce warning
  D9002 ("ignoring unknown option") with MSVC:

    - /arch:SSE4.2 for the sse42 CPU variant exists only in newer MSVC. MSVC
      19.29 (Visual Studio 2019, the AppVeyor image) ignores it for every
      source file of that variant. Add it only when check_c_compiler_flag
      accepts it; CMake treats D9002 as a failed check. Without the option the
      variant is compiled for SSE2 code generation, which is safe: MSVC accepts
      SSE4 intrinsics with any /arch, and the variant is chosen at run time only
      on CPUs with SSE4.2.
    - -fno-lto for the CPU feature detection objects is a GCC/clang option.
      Pass it only when not MSVC; MSVC does not use LTO unless /GL is given.

3. llama : fix a size_t truncation, and disable MSVC conversion warnings like ggml

  MSVC reports many C4244 ("possible loss of data") warnings in the llama,
  mtmd and other targets (for example std::fill of a float vector with 0.0 or
  0 in tools/mtmd/mtmd-audio.cpp, or std::pair<int64_t, uint32_t> from an
  int64_t in src/llama-model.cpp). Almost all are harmless and are the same in
  upstream llama.cpp. ggml/CMakeLists.txt already disables C4244, C4267 and
  C4305 (among others) for the ggml targets; do the same in the top-level
  CMakeLists.txt, before src, common and tools are added. MSVC only, so clang
  (the ARM64 build) is not affected.

  One of these warnings is a real truncation, fixed here:

    - src/llama-quant.cpp, llama_tensor_dequantize_impl: the worker lambda took
      the element count as int, but it is passed a size_t (thr_elems), and the
      functions it calls (to_float, ggml_fp16_to_fp32_row,
      ggml_bf16_to_fp32_row) take int64_t. A thread with more than 2^31 - 1
      elements (requantizing a very large tensor with few threads) would get a
      wrong count. Take int64_t.

Apply with: git -c core.autocrlf=false apply <this file>

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 81f23d7..d4a2b68 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -193,6 +193,16 @@ endif()
 # build the library
 #
 
+# MSVC: disable the conversion warnings that ggml/CMakeLists.txt also disables
+# for the ggml targets (MSVC_WARNING_FLAGS), for llama, common and the tools.
+if (MSVC)
+    add_compile_options(
+        /wd4244  # Conversion from one type to another type, possible loss of data
+        /wd4267  # Conversion from 'size_t' to a smaller type, possible loss of data
+        /wd4305  # Conversion from 'type1' to 'type2', possible loss of data
+    )
+endif()
+
 add_subdirectory(src)
 
 #
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
index 55f0f5a..6e0fec5 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13,7 +13,11 @@ function(ggml_add_cpu_backend_features cpu_name arch)
     # from inlining architecture-specific instructions into the score function.
     # Without this, LTO can cause SIGILL when loading backends on older CPUs
     # (e.g., loading power10 backend on power9 crashes before feature check runs).
-    target_compile_options(${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME} PRIVATE -fno-lto)
+    # -fno-lto is a GCC/clang option; MSVC warns about it (D9002) and does not
+    # use LTO unless /GL is given.
+    if (NOT MSVC)
+        target_compile_options(${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME} PRIVATE -fno-lto)
+    endif()
     target_link_libraries(${cpu_name} PRIVATE ${GGML_CPU_FEATS_NAME})
 endfunction()
 
@@ -300,7 +304,14 @@ function(ggml_add_cpu_backend_variant_impl tag_name)
                 list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:AVX)
                 list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS GGML_AVX)
             elseif (GGML_SSE42)
-                list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:SSE4.2)
+                # /arch:SSE4.2 exists only in newer MSVC; MSVC 19.29 (Visual
+                # Studio 2019) ignores it with warning D9002. The variant still
+                # builds without it: MSVC accepts SSE4 intrinsics with any /arch.
+                include(CheckCCompilerFlag)
+                check_c_compiler_flag("/arch:SSE4.2" GGML_MSVC_HAS_ARCH_SSE42)
+                if (GGML_MSVC_HAS_ARCH_SSE42)
+                    list(APPEND ARCH_FLAGS /arch:SSE4.2)
+                endif()
                 list(APPEND ARCH_DEFINITIONS GGML_SSE42)
             endif()
             if (GGML_AVX_VNNI)
diff --git a/src/llama-quant.cpp b/src/llama-quant.cpp
index c15bc7c..64773e1 100644
--- a/src/llama-quant.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-quant.cpp
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ static void llama_tensor_dequantize_impl(
         size_t thr_elems = thr_blocks * block_size; // number of elements for this thread
         size_t thr_block_bytes = thr_blocks * block_size_bytes; // number of input bytes for this thread
 
-        auto compute = [qtype] (ggml_type typ, uint8_t * inbuf, float * outbuf, int nels) {
+        auto compute = [qtype] (ggml_type typ, uint8_t * inbuf, float * outbuf, int64_t nels) {
             if (typ == GGML_TYPE_F16) {
                 ggml_fp16_to_fp32_row((ggml_fp16_t *)inbuf, outbuf, nels);
             } else if (typ == GGML_TYPE_BF16) {
diff --git a/tools/CMakeLists.txt b/tools/CMakeLists.txt
index 780df32..04441bf 100644
--- a/tools/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tools/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,3 +41,97 @@ else()
     add_subdirectory(fit-params)
     add_subdirectory(results)
 endif()
+
+# Windows resources for the tool executables:
+#   LLAMA_WIN_ICON         .ico file embedded as the application icon
+#   LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION  text for the version information shown in the file
+#                          properties, for example "llama.cpp built for WelsonJS":
+#                          the description becomes "<tool> (<text>)"
+set(LLAMA_WIN_ICON        "" CACHE FILEPATH "llama: .ico file embedded in the Windows tool executables")
+set(LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION "" CACHE STRING   "llama: text for the version information of the Windows tool executables")
+
+function(llama_collect_executables dir out)
+    get_property(targets DIRECTORY "${dir}" PROPERTY BUILDSYSTEM_TARGETS)
+    set(result "")
+    foreach (target IN LISTS targets)
+        get_target_property(type ${target} TYPE)
+        if (type STREQUAL "EXECUTABLE")
+            list(APPEND result ${target})
+        endif()
+    endforeach()
+    get_property(subdirs DIRECTORY "${dir}" PROPERTY SUBDIRECTORIES)
+    foreach (subdir IN LISTS subdirs)
+        llama_collect_executables("${subdir}" sub)
+        list(APPEND result ${sub})
+    endforeach()
+    set(${out} ${result} PARENT_SCOPE)
+endfunction()
+
+if (WIN32 AND (LLAMA_WIN_ICON OR LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION))
+    set(llama_win_res_dir "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/win-resources")
+    file(MAKE_DIRECTORY "${llama_win_res_dir}")
+
+    if (LLAMA_WIN_ICON)
+        if (NOT EXISTS "${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}")
+            message(FATAL_ERROR "LLAMA_WIN_ICON does not exist: ${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}")
+        endif()
+        # Copy the icon next to the resource scripts, which are UTF-8, so a path
+        # with non-ASCII characters does not depend on the ANSI code page.
+        configure_file("${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}" "${llama_win_res_dir}/llama-icon.ico" COPYONLY)
+    endif()
+
+    # Version numbers as in LLAMA_INSTALL_VERSION (0.0.<build number>).
+    set(llama_win_build "${LLAMA_BUILD_NUMBER}")
+    if (NOT llama_win_build MATCHES "^[0-9]+$")
+        set(llama_win_build 0)
+    endif()
+    # A double quote inside a resource string is written as two.
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_desc   "${LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION}")
+    string(REPLACE "\"" "\"\"" llama_win_commit "${LLAMA_BUILD_COMMIT}")
+
+    llama_collect_executables("${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}" llama_tool_executables)
+    foreach (target IN LISTS llama_tool_executables)
+        set(rc "#pragma code_page(65001)\n")
+        if (LLAMA_WIN_ICON)
+            string(APPEND rc "1 ICON \"${llama_win_res_dir}/llama-icon.ico\"\n")
+        endif()
+        if (LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION)
+            # Numeric values instead of winver.h names: 0x40004 = VOS_NT_WINDOWS32,
+            # 0x1 = VFT_APP, so no include path is needed (rc.exe and llvm-rc).
+            string(APPEND rc
+                "1 VERSIONINFO\n"
+                "FILEVERSION 0,0,${llama_win_build},0\n"
+                "PRODUCTVERSION 0,0,${llama_win_build},0\n"
+                "FILEFLAGSMASK 0x3F\n"
+                "FILEFLAGS 0x0\n"
+                "FILEOS 0x40004\n"
+                "FILETYPE 0x1\n"
+                "FILESUBTYPE 0x0\n"
+                "BEGIN\n"
+                "    BLOCK \"StringFileInfo\"\n"
+                "    BEGIN\n"
+                "        BLOCK \"040904B0\"\n"
+                "        BEGIN\n"
+                "            VALUE \"FileDescription\", \"${target} (${llama_win_desc})\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"FileVersion\", \"0.0.${llama_win_build}.0 (${llama_win_commit})\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"InternalName\", \"${target}\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"OriginalFilename\", \"${target}.exe\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"ProductName\", \"llama.cpp\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"ProductVersion\", \"0.0.${llama_win_build}.0 (${llama_win_commit})\"\n"
+                "            VALUE \"Comments\", \"${llama_win_desc}\"\n"
+                "        END\n"
+                "    END\n"
+                "    BLOCK \"VarFileInfo\"\n"
+                "    BEGIN\n"
+                "        VALUE \"Translation\", 0x409, 1200\n"
+                "    END\n"
+                "END\n")
+        endif()
+        # Write through configure_file, which only touches the file when it
+        # changes, so a new CMake run does not relink every tool.
+        file(WRITE "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc.in" "${rc}")
+        configure_file("${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc.in" "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc" COPYONLY)
+        target_sources(${target} PRIVATE "${llama_win_res_dir}/${target}.rc")
+    endforeach()
+    message(STATUS "Windows resources (icon: ${LLAMA_WIN_ICON}; description: ${LLAMA_WIN_DESCRIPTION}): ${llama_tool_executables}")
+endif()
